              "teach": "Four moves in one line, and each answers a specific refusal: <code>unhold</code> because apt will not touch a held package, <code>update</code> because the pinned version must be in the index, <code>--allow-downgrades</code> because going backwards is a deliberate act, and <code>hold</code> because unattended upgrades would otherwise undo all of it. Naming all three packages in one <code>install</code> also keeps them consistent — apt resolves them together rather than in three separate transactions."
